A||N||10||turbo86se||door removal||||5||
Z||000000||turbo86se||02-18-2000||04:47 PM||||<BR>Tomorrow my mechanic is going to be dropping off my 85 coupe to my house so I can start stripping the interior. It's a bright red coupe with near mint tan interior, that's the only reason why I bought it! I need to know the easiest way to remove the doors, so I can have better access in and out, besides that, they're in excellent shape! I plan on storing the dash, seats, carpet... etc <BR>Thanks for any help!!  -joel ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||02-18-2000||05:40 PM||||Piece of cake although they're heavier than heck!  Here goes:<BR>Step 1:  Drink a beer (or other beverage of your choice)<BR>Step 2:  Pop off the covers for the screws that hold the plastic trim pieces in front of the door and around the parking brake.  Remove the screws and trim.<BR>Step 3:  Drink another beer because the previous step will frustrate you.<BR>Step 4:  Pull the carpeting away from the front of the door opening.  Unplug the wiring harnesses (I think there are 2-main and p/m) and feel for a depression in the rubber that's attached to the side of the footwell.  Peel this off.<BR>Step 5:  Drink yet another beer.  (No real reason for this one.)<BR>Step 6:  Loosen but DO NOT REMOVE the 4 bolts.  (2 on the inside, another 2 on the hinge side-these are a b***h!)<BR>Step 7,8+9:  More beer.  You'll want them more than ever.  <BR>Step 10:  Place something hard yet soft (like a cinder block with a towel over it) under the door and finish removing the bolts.<BR>Step 11:  Finish the beers.  (You did buy a 12-pack, didn't you?)<BR>Step 12:  Place door gently against the wall.<BR>Step 15:  Stumble quietly (yeah, right!  You're bulletproof.) into the house and profusely apologize to your wife/significant other for spending the day in the garage, getting drunk and tracking mud into her clean house.<P>Hope this helps.  These are the steps I used when I dismantled my doors and I'm still happily married.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||02-18-2000||06:00 PM||||Monkeyman, What happened to 13 and 14? Were they used to get rid of the beverage of choice consumed in steps 1,3,5,7,8,9 and 11?||||reg||12
Z||000003||Phil||02-18-2000||06:43 PM||||OR    you could just undo the wiring connector and pull the hinge pins and be done with it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||02-18-2000||07:08 PM||||AHHH thats what I need, beer.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Eddie.H||02-18-2000||08:14 PM||||thats why monkeymans car has all that dirt on it after all that beer he forgets its dirty.||||reg||12
Z||000006||wkayl||02-18-2000||08:15 PM||||Mybe this will help troubleshoot any problems you may encounter:<P><BR>Beer Troubleshooting<P>SYMPTOM: Feet cold and wet.<BR>FAULT: Glass being held at incorrect angle.<BR>ACTION: Rotate glass so that open end points toward ceiling.<P>SYMPTOM: Beer unusually pale and tasteless.<BR>FAULT: Glass empty.<BR>ACTION: Get someone to buy you another beer.<P>SYMPTOM: Opposite wall covered with fluorescent lights.<BR>FAULT: You have fallen over backward.<BR>ACTION: Have yourself chained to bar.<P>SYMPTOM: Mouth contains cigarette butts.<BR>FAULT: You have fallen forward.<BR>ACTION: See above.<P>SYMPTOM: Beer tasteless, front of your shirt is wet.<BR>FAULT: Mouth not open, or glass applied to wrong part of face.<BR>ACTION: Retire to restroom, practice in mirror.<P>SYMPTOM: Floor blurred.<BR>FAULT: You are looking through bottom of empty glass.<BR>ACTION: Get someone to buy you another beer.<P>SYMPTOM: Floor moving.<BR>FAULT: You are being carried out.<BR>ACTION: Find out if you are being taken to another bar.<P>SYMPTOM: Room seems unusually dark.<BR>FAULT: Bar has closed.<BR>ACTION: Confirm home address with bartender, take taxi home.<P>SYMPTOM: Dashboard suddenly takes on colorful aspect and textures.<BR>FAULT: Beer consumption has exceeded personal limitations.<BR>ACTION: Cover mouth.<P>SYMPTOM: Everyone looks up to you and smiles.<BR>FAULT: You are dancing on the table.<BR>ACTION: Fall on somebody cushy-looking.<P>SYMPTOM: Your singing sounds distorted.<BR>FAULT: The beer is too weak.<BR>ACTION: Have more beer until your voice improves.<P>SYMPTOM: Don't remember the words to the song.<BR>FAULT: Beer is just right.<BR>ACTION: Play air guitar.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||02-18-2000||11:20 PM||||Where do I start?<BR>DRH--Steps 13 and 14 were accidentally left out due to steps 1,3,5,7,9 and 11.<P>Phil--I tried that and couldn't get the hinge pins out.  You'd have to compress the hinge springs and they're strong!  How'd you do it that way?  Besides, if you did it your way, how would you have an excuse to get bulletproof?<P>Eddie--It's not that I forget it's dirty, but just that I decide it's not worth getting up off of the couch for. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>wkayl--very good.  2 thumbs up.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Phil||02-18-2000||11:40 PM||||I just popped the spring off with a screw driver and knocked the pins out. Putting the doors back on by just doing the pins would be a whole other ball game for I don't think you could get the spring back in. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||turbo86se||02-19-2000||01:15 AM||||LOL!  Monkeyman,that's the best advice I've heard yet! I watched my mechanic remove my door to my coupe once, on step 10, instead of putting a block under the door, he shut it, removed the bolts, and removed the door easily. Do I have to take the fender off? Wait a minute, the entire front end is stripped! Forget that last question!  If I follow monkeyman's steps, by step 10, I'll be so drunk, I'll be lucky if I don't start removing the rear decklid! "This door sure does look funny!" hicup!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I'd offer this thing for parts, but there really isn't anything that's of value, especially after I strip the interior. The engine has a rod knock, but will start. If anyone has any more pointers or shortcuts, please LMK! thanks again, joel ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Monkeyman||02-19-2000||01:56 AM||||Phil--I never thought of doing that.  Good idea, but then there would be no reason to have a beer (although you don't need a reason).||||reg||1
